Z||000000||triker||04-25-2000||07:12 PM||||I'm having problems with my 85 automatic 2.8 under w.o.t.  It Falls on it's face at the point when it is (or should be) shifting from 1st to 2nd.  If I ease off just a little before I think it's going to quit, it shifts just fine.  After it dies I have to let off on the throttle before it'll start going again.  I've played with the down shift cable, but it doesn't seem to help.  Any have any ideas?  Triker    P.S.  The reason I use Triker is that one of my Feiros only has 3 wheels.                   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sdm1964||04-25-2000||08:56 PM||||I would say try changing the fluid and filter. You know it is manditory to post pics of your fieros. And you already have more than one, well get to posting... that would be my next try filter and fluid.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Raydar||04-25-2000||09:43 PM||||Triker, What RPM does it shift at? Left in "D", mine shifts at around 5000 RPM, usually. Almost sounds like you're hitting a rev limiter. (That's assuming that the automatic *has* a rev limiter. Don't know for sure.) If you hadn't already tried it, I would say "adjust the TV (kickdown) cable."<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||04-25-2000||11:23 PM||||The RPM limiter kicks in at 6000 and back out at 4000. If you are hitting the limiter like that, I would check the TV cable first to see if it's holding it in gear.<P>1. Depress and hold down the metal readjust tab at the end of the TV cable.<BR>2. Move the slider until it stops agaist the fitting.<BR>3. Release the adjustment tab.<BR>4. Rotate the throttle lever to its full travel position (wide open).<BR>5. The slider must move (ratchet) towards the lever when the lever is rotated to its full travel position (wide open throttle).<P>When misadjusted, it will change the shifting dramtically.<P>From the manual.....||||reg||1
Z||000004||triker||04-26-2000||11:57 AM||||I don't have a tach on my Fiero trike (it's the one with the problem), but comparing it with my 87GT, I'd guess it dies at about 4000 rpm.  I'd like to know more about the rev limiter.  Where's it located and what does it look like?  Is it in the ECM?||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||04-26-2000||07:31 PM||||The revlimiter (like the speed limiter) is in the ECM code. It's disabled on 86-88 7170 ECM's.||||reg||1
Z||000006||triker||04-26-2000||08:15 PM||||I guess I need to hook up a temporary tach and see at what rpm it's cutting out at.  Since it's an 85 it could be the rev limiter, but it doesn't feel like its any where near 6000.||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||04-27-2000||01:49 PM||||I was just thinking on what could hold it in gear long enough to hit the limiter. The TV cable can if the adjustment is very bad.<P>My 86 SE auto shifts at 5000 (someone pointed out).<P>Well, see what the RPM is when it chokes.<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fret Naught||04-27-2000||03:08 PM||||Don't know what Fiero's have on them, or why Fiero's have AT or why never mind, went through a very similar problem recently on my wife's van. Turned out to be the Vacume modulater. Cheap and easy fix.||||reg||1
